# Tests

When the user asks to create tests, use the matching project skill and obey path rules under `.cursor/rules/`:

| Request | Skill | Rules |
| ------- | ----- | ----- |
| Manual / QA checklist | `manual-test-case-author` | `manual-test-cases.mdc` |
| API / endpoint / cy.request | `api-test-author` | `api-tests.mdc` |
| E2E / Cypress + Playwright live UI | `e2e-test-author` | `e2e-tests.mdc` |
| Mock UI / intercept + route | `mock-ui-test-author` | `mock-ui-tests.mdc` |
| Page object / POM | `page-object-author` | `page-objects.mdc` |
| Screen object (Appium) | `screen-object-author` | `screen-objects.mdc` |
| Mock component / Jest page test | `mock-component-test-author` | `mock-component-tests.mdc` |
| iOS e2e / Appium / Simulator | `ios-e2e-test-author` | `ios-e2e-tests.mdc` |
| Android e2e / Appium / Emulator | `android-e2e-test-author` | `android-e2e-tests.mdc` |

API, e2e, and mock-ui skills write **both Cypress and Playwright** unless the user names one framework. Prefer existing patterns over inventing new ones.

## Manual → automation handoff

When the user says a manual case is **done**, **complete**, **ready to automate**, or asks to **write API/e2e/mock/iOS/Android tests from** a `docs/test-cases/*.md` file:

1. Read that markdown file.
2. Split cases by layer:
   - **API** — HTTP status/body (login, list orders empty, etc.) → follow `api-test-author` (shared web + iOS; no separate iOS API suite)
   - **E2E** — Cypress/Playwright browser UI against the live API → follow `e2e-test-author`
   - **Mock UI** — browser UI with `cy.intercept` / `page.route` → follow `mock-ui-test-author` (specs under `e2e/mock-ui/`)
   - **Mock component** — Jest component empty/loading/error with mocked API → follow `mock-component-test-author`
   - **iOS e2e** — Simulator-visible customer flows → follow `ios-e2e-test-author`
   - **Android e2e** — Emulator-visible customer flows → follow `android-e2e-test-author`
3. Skip or note cases that are exploratory-only / not automatable.
4. Prefer extending shared fixtures for API; keep Cypress and Playwright in sync.

