## Web selectors

- Prefer `data-testid` in UI, e2e, and manual steps.
- Avoid CSS class / text-only selectors unless no test id exists (then add a test id in the product code).

## File placement

| Kind                | Location                                                         |
| ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Manual              | `docs/test-cases/*.md`                                           |
| Cypress API         | `cypress/tests/api/*.cy.ts`                                      |
| Cypress e2e         | `cypress/tests/e2e/*.cy.ts`                                      |
| Cypress mock UI     | `cypress/tests/e2e/mock-ui/*.cy.ts` (`cy.intercept`)             |
| Cypress PO          | `cypress/pages/` (required for e2e / mock UI)                    |
| API fixtures        | `cypress/fixtures/endpoints/`, `cypress/fixtures/models/`        |
| Binary fixtures     | `fixtures/` (e.g. images)                                        |
| Playwright API      | `playwright/api/*.spec.ts`                                       |
| Playwright e2e      | `playwright/e2e/*.spec.ts` (or `playwright/*.spec.ts` until moved) |
| Playwright mock UI  | `playwright/e2e/mock-ui/*.spec.ts` (`page.route`)                |
| Playwright PO       | `playwright/pages/*.page.ts` (required for e2e / mock UI)        |
| Playwright auth     | `playwright/support/login.ts`                                    |
| Mock component      | next to source as `*.test.tsx`                                   |
| Appium specs        | `appium/specs/*.spec.ts` (shared iOS + Android)                  |
| Appium screens      | `appium/screens/*.screen.ts`                                     |
| iOS SwiftUI app     | `ios/Marlow/Marlow/`                                             |
| Android Compose app | `android/Marlow/app/src/main/`                                   |

## How to run

| Suite             | Command                                  |
| ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Unit / mock component | `npm run test:unit`                  |
| Cypress API       | `npm run cypress:api`                    |
| Cypress e2e       | `npm run cypress:e2e`                    |
| Cypress Docker    | `npm run cypress:docker`                 |
| Playwright API    | `npm run playwright:api`                 |
| Playwright e2e    | `npx playwright test --project=chromium` |
| Playwright Docker | `npm run playwright:docker`              |
| Appium iOS        | `npm run appium:ios`                     |
| Appium Android    | `npm run appium:android`                 |

Docker runners boot the shop via `scripts/e2e-up.sh` and use `host.docker.internal`. Only change Vite `LISTEN_HOST` / `E2E_HOST` / `allowedHosts` when fixing Docker reachability—not for ordinary new tests.

## Layer pointers

- **API** (schema, fixtures, Cypress/Playwright HTTP asserts) → `api-tests.mdc`
- **Browser e2e** (live API, page objects, login helpers) → `e2e-tests.mdc`
- **Mock UI** (browser + `cy.intercept` / `page.route`) → `mock-ui-tests.mdc` / `mock-ui-test-author`
- **Mock component** (Jest) → `mock-component-tests.mdc` / `mock-component-test-author`
- **Page objects** (Cypress/Playwright) → `page-objects.mdc` / `page-object-author`
- **Screen objects** (Appium) → `screen-objects.mdc` / `screen-object-author`
- **iOS e2e** (flows + accessibility ids) → `ios-e2e-tests.mdc`. Keep Swift `Models` aligned with fixtures/OpenAPI; HTTP contracts stay in shared API suites.
- **Android e2e** (Compose + accessibility ids) → `android-e2e-tests.mdc`. Keep Kotlin models aligned with iOS/fixtures; HTTP contracts stay in shared API suites.
